# Force LF everywhere, regardless of the checking-out OS's core.autocrlf.
# Two concrete reasons this matters, not just tidiness:
#  - A CRLF shebang line (`#!/usr/bin/env bash\r`) fails with "bad
#    interpreter" wherever a script is executed directly (git hooks, CI).
#  - PHPCS's Generic.Files.LineEndings sniff flags CRLF as an error — on a
#    Windows checkout with the default core.autocrlf=true, every PHP file
#    would otherwise get checked out with CRLF and fail lint on line 1 of
#    every single file before any real sniff even runs.
* text=auto eol=lf
